        <owl:annotatedTarget>Stellate neurons are a specialized type of interneurons found predominantly in the cerebral cortex and the cerebellum, two major components of the brain&apos;s central nervous system. These neurons are named for their distinct star-like shape, characterized by short dendrites that radiate from the cell body in multiple directions. They are a key component of the mammalian neural circuit due to their unique morphology and crucial functions in neural communication.
