        <obo:IAO_0000115>The process in which an antigenically naive T cell acquires the specialized features of an effector, regulatory, or memory T cell as part of an immune response. Effector T cells include cells which provide T cell help or exhibit cytotoxicity towards other cells.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment>Note that immunologists typically use the word &apos;development&apos; to refer to cells of B or T cell lineages undergoing the process that GO describes as &apos;cell differentiation&apos;.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>T cell differentiation involved in immune response</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
