        <obo:IAO_0000115>The process in which a precursor cell type acquires the specialized features of a dendritic cell. A dendritic cell is a leukocyte of dendritic lineage specialized in the uptake, processing, and transport of antigens to lymph nodes for the purpose of stimulating an immune response via T cell activation.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <rdfs:comment>Note that immunologists typically use the word &apos;maturation&apos; to refer to dendritic cells undergoing the process that GO describes as &apos;cell differentiation&apos;.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>dendritic cell differentiation</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
